DeviceChain instance root-key escrow (ADR-059)
==============================================

This file is the ONLY copy of the key that decrypts secrets stored by
DeviceChain instance "golden-prod" outside that instance's own cluster. It is NOT
contained in any database backup: the key lives in the cluster's etcd, which
database backups do not cover.

If this file and its passphrase are lost, every secret the instance has stored
-- connector credentials, SMTP passwords, AI provider keys -- becomes
permanently unrecoverable after a restore to a new cluster. Restoring the
databases will appear to succeed and the secrets will not decrypt.

Store this file and its passphrase OFF-CLUSTER, and separately from each
other. To recover, seed a rebuilt instance from this file BEFORE restoring
its databases:

  dcctl bootstrap <provider> golden-prod --restore-root-key <this file>

  instance:     golden-prod
  created:      2026-07-26T21:00:00Z
  kdf:          argon2id t=1 m=8KiB p=1
  cipher:       AES-256-GCM
  key id:       d444f2cf32d3398e6c7fcd0f8825d4f9a672b332d9036982e1e286472bcdcb1e

